<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

  <!-- Settings: window category (mod-list entry) -->
  <!-- EN: Unique Melee Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsCategory>特化近战武器</UMW_SettingsCategory>

  <!-- Settings: section headers. Only the headers with no vanilla-localized equivalent live here:
       the Abilities header reuses Core's Keyed <Abilities> string and the Quests header reuses the
       quests main-tab button's def label (MainButtonDefOf.Quests), so both arrive pre-translated in
       every language and must not be duplicated in this file. -->
  <!-- EN: Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsWeapons>武器</UMW_SettingsWeapons>

  <!-- EN: Generation -->
  <UMW_SettingsGeneration>生成</UMW_SettingsGeneration>

  <!-- Settings: reusable label suffixes. Each includes a leading space, and every applicable one is
       appended (no precedence between them), so they must read cleanly back to back. -->
  <!-- EN:  (default) -->
  <UMW_DefaultSuffix>（默认）</UMW_DefaultSuffix>

  <!-- {0} is another piece of content the current value matches, named from its own def label. -->
  <!-- EN:  (same as {0}) -->
  <UMW_SameAsSuffix>（与“{0}”相同）</UMW_SameAsSuffix>

  <!-- Settings: Weapons. One checkbox per weapon, labelled from the weapon's own def label; the row list
       is generated, so this is the only string it needs. {0} is that label (lowercase).
       "This mod's own ... and every vanilla" is a deliberate qualifier, not filler: the gate covers every
       pool that asks ThingSetMakerUtility, which is all shipped content, but a third-party mod rolling
       loot through its own custom generator can bypass it (see ThingSetMakerUtility_CanGenerate_Patch.cs). -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to be generated. Turn off to remove it from this mod's own reward pool and from every vanilla generation and reward pool, including quest rewards, ancient crates, item stashes and map loot, so it no longer appears. (A third-party mod that rolls loot through its own custom generator may bypass this.) Any that already exist in your save are untouched, and the other weapons take its place in the rolls. Turning it back on is enough to restore it. -->
  <UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>允许生成“{0}”。关闭后，该武器会从本模组自身的奖励池以及原版的所有生成池和奖励池中移除，包括任务奖励、密封储物箱、物品藏匿点和地图战利品，此后不会再出现。（通过自带生成器分配战利品的第三方模组可能绕过此设置。）存档中已有的该武器不受影响，其余武器会在抽取中顶替它的位置。重新开启即可将其恢复。</UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: buttons -->
  <!-- EN: Reset to defaults -->
  <UMW_ResetToDefaults>重置为默认值</UMW_ResetToDefaults>

  <!-- Settings: Generation -->
  <!-- {0} is the wood resource's item label (ThingDef WoodLog, "wood" in English, lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Exclude {0} from generated unique weapons -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>生成特化武器时排除“{0}”</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>

  <!-- {0} is the vanilla longsword's item label (lowercase), named as the example reward. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons only enter the game through generated rewards (quests, ancient crates, item stashes), rolled from a random eligible material. With this on, wooden materials are dropped from that roll, so a hard-won reward never lands as a wooden {0}. Turn off to allow wooden uniques. -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>特化武器只能通过生成的奖励（任务、密封储物箱、物品藏匿点）进入游戏，其材料从符合条件的材料中随机抽取。开启后，木质材料会被排除在抽取之外，来之不易的奖励就不会是一把木制“{0}”。关闭以允许木制的特化武器。</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>

  <!-- Shown only when Royalty is active; the traits it governs need that DLC.
       {0}, {1}, {2} are the three trait labels (lowercase): monomolecular, plasma-cored, zeus-headed.
       Each parenthetical describes the trait injected just before it, so keep them paired. -->
  <!-- EN: Allow ultratech weapon traits -->
  <UMW_AllowUltratechTraits>允许极致科技武器特性</UMW_AllowUltratechTraits>

  <!-- EN: Three traits borrow Royalty's ultratech melee kit: {0} (a mechanite-held edge that shears armor), {1} (a plasma sheath that sears and ignites) and {2} (an EMP discharge that stuns mechanoids). Turn off to keep them out of the roll. This is meant for medieval-only or low-tech runs, where a mechanite edge on a hand-forged sword breaks the period. The other traits are unaffected, and weapons that have already rolled one of these keep it. -->
  <UMW_AllowUltratechTraitsDesc>三项特性借用了“皇权”的极致科技近战装备：“{0}”（由纳米机械维持的刃口，可切开护甲）、“{1}”（等离子体护层，会灼伤并点燃目标）和“{2}”（EMP放电，可击晕机械族）。关闭后它们不再参与抽取。此设置面向纯中世纪或低科技的游戏流程，在那样的时代背景下，手工锻造的剑上出现纳米机械刃口会破坏时代感。其余特性不受影响，已经抽到这些特性的武器会保留它们。</UMW_AllowUltratechTraitsDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Abilities. Slider labels are shared templates: {0} is the subject's own def label
       (an ability, a hediff, or the warband faction), capitalized; {1} is the slider's current value.
       The unit word is part of the template, so hour- and day-based cooldowns are separate keys. -->
  <!-- EN: {0} cooldown: {1} hours -->
  <UMW_AbilityCooldownHours>{0}冷却时间：{1}小时</UMW_AbilityCooldownHours>

  <!-- EN: {0} cooldown: {1} days -->
  <UMW_AbilityCooldownDays>{0}冷却时间：{1}天</UMW_AbilityCooldownDays>

  <!-- EN: {0} radius: {1} cells -->
  <UMW_AbilityRadius>{0}半径：{1}格</UMW_AbilityRadius>

  <!-- EN: {0} duration: {1} hours -->
  <UMW_HediffDurationHours>{0}持续时间：{1}小时</UMW_HediffDurationHours>

  <!-- EN: How long a piledriver weapon must rest between earthshakes. The default matches the cooldown on the EMP pulser, the one weapon-trait ability Odyssey ships with a cooldown. Set to 0 for no cooldown at all. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>装有打桩头的武器在两次撼地之间需要休整多久。默认值与“EMP脉冲发生器”的冷却时间一致，后者是奥德赛中唯一自带冷却时间的武器特性能力。设为0则完全没有冷却时间。</UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the stunning shockwave reaches. It travels through the ground, so walls do not stop it, but it cannot cross a gap with no floor. The overhead ripple scales to match. Remember the shock is indiscriminate: a wider radius catches more of your own colonists too. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>造成击晕的冲击波能波及多远。冲击波沿地面传播，墙壁无法阻挡它，但它无法越过没有地面的裂隙。地表上方的涟漪特效会随半径一同缩放。请记住，震击不分敌我：半径越大，殃及的自家殖民者也越多。</UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: How long a storied weapon must rest between rallying cries. Measured in days rather than hours on purpose: the default makes it an heirloom moment rather than a standing aura you re-apply every fight. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>传世武器在两次鼓舞呐喊之间需要休整多久。刻意以天而非小时计量：默认值使呐喊成为传家宝般的难得时刻，而不是每场战斗都重新施放的常驻光环。</UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the cry carries. It rallies every humanlike within this range who is not hostile to the wielder and can see them, so allied and neutral pawns are included but walls and closed doors block it. Waking sleepers uses the same range but ignores walls, and catches enemies as well. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>呐喊能传多远。范围内所有对使用者不怀敌意且能看见使用者的人类都会受到鼓舞，因此盟友和中立角色也包括在内，但墙壁和关闭的门会挡住呐喊。唤醒沉睡者使用同一范围，但无视墙壁，也会一并惊醒敌人。</UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: How long the rallied buff lasts on each pawn the cry reaches, halving both their pain and the time a hit staggers them. Anyone who was asleep is woken instead of rallied, and resents it. Changing this affects cries made from now on; anyone already rallied keeps the duration they were given. -->
  <UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>士气大振效果在呐喊触及的每个角色身上持续多久：疼痛和受击后脚步被打乱的时间都减半。睡着的人不会受到鼓舞，而是被吵醒，并为此心生不满。修改只影响之后发出的呐喊；已受鼓舞者保留原有的持续时间。</UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Quests. The slider label reuses the shared template pattern: {0} is the warband
       faction's def label (capitalized), {1} the value. The desc's quest examples (ancient
       mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes) are vanilla content names; translate them to match
       the official localization. -->
  <!-- EN: {0} quest commonality: {1} -->
  <UMW_QuestWeight>{0}任务出现频率：{1}</UMW_QuestWeight>

  <!-- EN: Selection weight of the warband quest against the other opportunity-site quests (ancient mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes...) offered by traders, beggars and reading. Higher = offered more often. 0 disables the quest entirely. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>战团任务相对于其他同类地点任务（古代雇佣兵、匪徒营地、物品藏匿点……）的选取权重，这类任务可通过商人、行乞者和阅读获得。数值越高，出现越频繁。设为0则完全禁用该任务。</UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>

</LanguageData>
